@H H_1169 := "semantic×surface surplus — is S maximal at the high-sem/LOW-surf corner ('같은 내용 다른 표현')?" :: MITOSIS-ENGINE [terminal]
  verdict      = "🔴 CORNER-NOT-SINGLED-OUT (closed-negative, a_paper_negative_ok)"
  seed         = "H_1167 super-additive surplus S=whole−Σparts; sharpen: does S peak at HIGH-semantic/LOW-surface (same content, different form = '어울림'+'어긋남'), beating BOTH redundancy (P1 identical) AND unrelatedness (P5)? + abstraction (P4) angle"
  domain       = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"
  substrate    = "Lane-G/CORE reference (faithful-φ engine + H_1116 content-ngram); REAL 5-lang c4 parallel data + flores en"
  method       = "g5/p7 $0 CPU 0-pod deterministic 12 seeds; 6 pre-reg pair-types (sem,surf frozen): P1 identical / P2 paraphrase-proxy(syn-map+reorder,TOY) / P3 cross-lingual parallel(REAL same-meaning) / P4 abstraction stem-skeleton(TOY) / P5 unrelated / P6 random-bytes; 2 measures: (a) S_phi faithful-φ on byte-bucket co-occ rep [PROXY] · (b) S_recomb H_1116 content-ngram [p7]"
  falsifier    = "🟢 iff, per measure, argmax∈HSLS{P2,P3,P4} AND S(WIN)−S(P1) d≥0.8 AND S(WIN)−S(P5) d≥0.8 on BOTH measures; 🔴 if neither measure singles out the high-sem/low-surf corner"

  # ── RESULT (verbatim .verdicts/1169_semantic_surface_surplus/H_1169.txt) ──
  result_phi   = "measure (a) S_phi DEGENERATE — faithful φ_EI reads ~0 (max|mean|=2.97e-9 < 1e-4) on a STATIC short-text byte rep; the φ-surplus machinery wants a DYNAMICAL rollout (H_1167 A⇄G substrate) and does NOT transfer to static text pairs → flagged DEGENERATE, NOT counted (a_phi_iit4_tool: don't trust a flat proxy). SUPPORTED=False (forced)."
  result_recomb= "measure (b) S_recomb WIN=P2_paraphrase (∈HSLS, C1 PASS), S(P2)−S(P1) d=+9.45 (C2 PASS) BUT S(P2)−S(P5) d=+0.000 (C3 FAIL — P2 paraphrase +3.0 == P5 unrelated +3.0 mean; the corner does NOT beat unrelatedness). SUPPORTED=False."
  map_2d       = "S_recomb means: P1=−5.33 (redundant, words add nothing) · P2=+3.0 · P3=+0.000 (cross-lingual!) · P4=−4.0 (abstraction) · P5=+3.0 · P6=+0.33"
  surface_track= "S_recomb tracks SURFACE not SEMANTICS: corr(S,surf_proxy)=−0.54 > corr(S,sem_proxy)=−0.47. P3 cross-lingual (the ONLY fully-REAL same-meaning pair) reads +0.000 because the recomb metric is English-DICT-lexical and structurally BLIND to non-Latin script — exactly the H_1155 surface-dominance caveat made visible."
  abstraction  = "abstraction P4 does NOT peak (S_recomb=−4.0, NEGATIVE) — stem-skeleton REMOVES coherent n-grams rather than creating new combos; abstraction-gap ≠ surplus source."
  winning_form = "no form-type wins the falsifier; the 'WIN' by raw mean (P2 paraphrase, surface-driven) is a surface-novelty artifact, not a semantic-corner win"

  finding      = "RULES OUT 'same-content-different-form maximizes super-additive surplus' at toy scale on these reps. The recombination surplus is a SURFACE-NOVELTY measure (new lexical n-grams), NOT a semantic-fit measure: it cannot see cross-lingual same-meaning (P3→0, script-blind) and abstraction REDUCES it (P4<0). The φ-surplus is DEGENERATE on static text (needs a dynamical substrate). NEITHER measure singles out the high-sem/low-surf corner. CONSISTENT with H_1155 (toy byte/lexical reps are surface-dominated; no semantic alignment at toy scale)."
  honest       = "P2/P4 = DETERMINISTIC toy proxies (synonym-map / stem-skeleton), NOT human-labeled paraphrase/abstraction; P3 cross-lingual = the only fully-REAL same-meaning pairing, and it's the one the recomb metric is BLIND to. S_phi = faithful-φ engine on a BYTE rep = PROXY, and it's DEGENERATE here. C3 d=0 reflects zero-variance deterministic surpluses (honest null, not a power gap). Toy scale; a LEARNED cross-lingual semantic rep + a DYNAMICAL φ substrate UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope)."
  files        = "UNIVERSE/h1169_semantic_surface_surplus.py · .verdicts/1169_semantic_surface_surplus/H_1169.txt · .verdicts/1169_semantic_surface_surplus/verdict.json"
  xref         = "h1167 (surplus peaks at criticality — the parent) · h1155 (interlingua semantic alignment NULL, surface-dominated — confirmed here) · h1168 (1-D distance ladder sibling) · h1116 (content-ngram recombination metric) · a_phi_iit4_tool · a_scale_honest_scope · a_paper_negative_ok · p7"
